body:
## Problem and responsibility

A successful Formal AI idle update is discarded when the next task acquires the sidecar. This is in Hive Mind's lifecycle composition, not image publication or Agent CLI execution.

I reproduced this against current main `3ed0eeff91d8d43a4056d0176374d478a49060e2`. The relevant `formal-ai-sidecar.lib.mjs` is byte-identical in deployed Hive Mind v2.15.1 (`c0d9725d6527cc084ab10b4d78c909b108cfde9f`).

## Production evidence

On September 4, 2026, Formal AI v0.346.0 was published at 19:09 UTC. Independent anonymous registry checks confirmed that its versioned image and `:latest` matched digest `sha256:0c513fa777ffea50901f6b35e575a8be2b24e2588989cc17173805b0c7cf50a0`, with all 59 layers accessible.

Later attempts delivered no implementation:
- [Rust / Codex](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb331-c107-78c7-8ff6-9f127a3c593c/pull/2#issuecomment-5547362635): only the placeholder commit/file remains.
- [Kotlin / Claude](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-fa49-7c9d-a664-b7ea33bb698a/pull/2#issuecomment-5547379361): zero-file PR, terminal `planned_not_executed`.
- [Scala / Agent](https://github.com/konard/test-hello-world-019fb330-00e1-73b9-955e-f357a1600d5b/pull/2#issuecomment-5547506651): zero-file PR, terminal `planned_not_executed`.

The emitted one-step write-only repository plan matches older Formal AI behavior; v0.346.0's `compose_repository_work_plan` includes a Fetch step before Write. These task logs do **not** establish the serving image's exact version: their `Formal AI: version 0.339.1` comes from the local wrapper probe. They also lack the host updater/lease logs needed to prove this exact lifecycle transition happened on that host. The defect below is independently reproduced, rather than inferred solely from those logs.

## Exact root cause

1. [updateFormalAiSidecarWhenIdle](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/3ed0eeff91d8d43a4056d0176374d478a49060e2/src/formal-ai-updater.lib.mjs) pulls latest, verifies memory compatibility and serving health, stops the idle sidecar, and writes the accepted image/digest into state.
2. [acquireFormalAiSidecar](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/3ed0eeff91d8d43a4056d0176374d478a49060e2/src/formal-ai-sidecar.lib.mjs#L333) reads that state, but its image selection uses only a running container or `ensureFormalAiSidecarImage({env, ...})`. It never supplies the accepted `state.image`/`state.imageDigest`.
3. [resolveFormalAiSidecarImageCandidates](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/3ed0eeff91d8d43a4056d0176374d478a49060e2/src/formal-ai-image.lib.mjs) therefore chooses the bootstrap version again (currently 0.345.0).
4. Acquiring the task overwrites state with the old digest. A verified update can consequently never persist into the next cold task.

## Executed failing regression

Save as `reproduce-update-acquire.mjs` at the Hive Mind repository root and run `node reproduce-update-acquire.mjs`. No dependencies, real Docker daemon, registry downloads, or production memory are needed. It exercises the unchanged production lifecycle/updater using the repository's existing Docker simulator.

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import os from 'node:os';
import path from 'node:path';
import { updateFormalAiSidecarWhenIdle } from './src/formal-ai-updater.lib.mjs';
import { acquireFormalAiSidecar, readFormalAiSidecarState, writeFormalAiSidecarState } from './src/formal-ai-sidecar.lib.mjs';
import { FORMAL_AI_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION } from './src/formal-ai-version.lib.mjs';
import { createDockerSimulator } from './tests/formal-ai-docker-simulator.mjs';

const stateDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'formal-ai-update-acquire-'));
const env = { HIVE_MIND_STATE_DIR: stateDir };
const repository = 'ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai';
const bootstrap = `${repository}:${FORMAL_AI_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION}`;
const latest = `${repository}:latest`;
const memory = { compatible: true, schema_version: 2, migration_required: false, migration_state: 'current' };
const docker = createDockerSimulator({
  images: { [bootstrap]: 'sha256:old' },
  pull: { [latest]: 'sha256:new' },
  health: image => ({ version: image === latest ? '0.346.0' : FORMAL_AI_BOOTSTRAP_VERSION, memory }),
  memory: { 'upgrade-status': { ...memory, path_exists: false } },
});
const options = { env, run: docker.run, healthAttempts: 1, healthDelayMs: 0, sleepImpl: async () => {} };
try {
  writeFormalAiSidecarState({ image: bootstrap, imageDigest: 'sha256:old', leases: [] }, { env });
  const update = await updateFormalAiSidecarWhenIdle(options);
  assert.equal(update.status, 'updated');
  assert.equal(readFormalAiSidecarState({ env }).imageDigest, 'sha256:new');
  const task = await acquireFormalAiSidecar({ sessionId: 'release-verification-task', ...options });
  console.log(JSON.stringify({ updateStatus: update.status, updatedVersion: update.health.version,
    updatedDigest: update.digest, taskImage: task.image, taskVersion: task.health.version,
    taskDigest: task.imageDigest }, null, 2));
  assert.equal(task.imageDigest, update.digest, 'the next task must consume the successfully verified update');
} finally {
  fs.rmSync(stateDir, { recursive: true, force: true });
}
```

Observed:
```json
{"updateStatus":"updated","updatedVersion":"0.346.0","updatedDigest":"sha256:new","taskImage":"ghcr.io/link-assistant/formal-ai:0.345.0","taskVersion":"0.345.0","taskDigest":"sha256:old"}
```
The final assertion fails with actual `sha256:old`, expected `sha256:new`.

Existing `test-issue-2146-formal-ai-lifecycle.mjs`, `test-issue-2146-idle-updates.mjs`, and `test-issue-2154-formal-ai-image-resolution.mjs` all pass: their coverage does not compose successful update with next-task acquisition.

## Fix contract and acceptance

- [ ] A cold task must consume the last accepted, verified image identity. Treat the pin as bootstrap only when no accepted state exists; explicit operator pins remain authoritative.
- [ ] Prefer the accepted immutable digest, so a moving tag cannot bypass memory verification after acceptance.
- [ ] Preserve active leases, memory backup/rollback semantics, and failure diagnostics. Do not silently fall back to an older binary against migrated memory.
- [ ] Add the update → stopped sidecar → acquire → release → acquire regression, including process restart with persisted state, rollback, unavailable accepted image, explicit pin, and a busy lease.
- [ ] Run the real published image through the same transition and record the leased server's health version and digest.
- [ ] Then replay the three referenced tasks through their real clients. Assert issue body/comments were read, requested source **and GitHub Actions workflow** were written in the clone, exact output tests passed, a non-placeholder commit was pushed, and the remote PR diff contains the implementation. An update status or zero client exit alone is not completion.

This test must not be solved by hardcoding a release number; selection must follow the verified state.

Related reports: [serving-version provenance #2208](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/2208), [Formal AI tool scope and argument grounding #1075](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/1075).
